{
  "_why": "The PowerShell library's ACTUAL answers to the four rules that decide which boundary owns a path. Captured once, by running `lib/VerificationBoundaries.ps1`, immediately before that file was deleted in the same commit that added this fixture. A cross-implementation differential cannot outlive its oracle, but its ANSWERS are data and data can be committed.",
  "_what_this_does_not_prove": "It cannot detect a case that was never asked. A live differential discovers bugs by asking questions; a golden only answers questions already recorded, so a rule that changes only on an unasked case is now invisible. That is the class the live comparison used to catch, and the loss is real.",
  "_oracle": "scripts/lib/VerificationBoundaries.ps1 (deleted in the same commit)",
